# Settings page pattern

## Layout structure

Settings pages live under `/settings/*` and share `src/app/settings/layout.tsx` which renders:
- Left: narrow nav rail (`w-56`) with links to Overview / AI / Reports
- Right: full remaining panel (`flex-1 overflow-y-auto`)

## Page content wrapper

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — matches other full-panel pages (/portfolio, /analysis, /news)
<div className="space-y-6 p-6">
  <div>
    <h1 className="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--fg)]">Page title</h1>
    <p className="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">Description</p>
  </div>
  {/* content */}
</div>

// ❌ WRONG — constrains width, breaks full-panel design
<div className="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 p-6">
```

## Server/client split

```
src/app/settings/[section]/page.tsx  ← Server component
  - auth() check → redirect("/login")
  - read server-side data (getLlmStatus, DB)
  - render layout with <ClientPanel />

src/components/settings/[name]-panel.tsx  ← "use client"
  - own state, fetch /api/settings/*, save logic
  - localStorage for client-only prefs (report settings)
  - Neon via API for shared/cross-device prefs (AI settings)
```

## API endpoints

```
src/app/api/settings/[section]/route.ts
  GET  → return user settings (auth required)
  PUT  → save user settings (auth required)
```

## DB key for settings in ai_response_cache

`symbol` is VARCHAR(16) — always keep the key ≤ 16 chars:
- AI config: `symbol="_ai_cfg_"`, `analysisType="ai_config"`, `modelName=userId`
- Other sections: follow same pattern with a short symbol key

## New section checklist

1. Add nav item to `settings/layout.tsx`
2. Create `settings/[section]/page.tsx` (server, auth guard)
3. Create `components/settings/[name]-panel.tsx` (client)
4. Create `api/settings/[section]/route.ts` (GET + PUT)
5. Use `p-6 space-y-6` wrapper — no `max-w-*`
